.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_DC_DEVI_CREATE 9F
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_dc_devi_create
.Nd construct a child from a device-control property list
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_dc_devi_create
.Fa "struct devctl_iocdata *dcp"
.Fa "dev_info_t *pdip"
.Fa "int flags"
.Fa "dev_info_t **rdip"
.Fc
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va dcp
Copied device-control request containing the property nvlist.
.It Va pdip
Parent nexus for the new child.
.It Va flags
Use \fBDEVCTL_CONSTRUCT\fP to stop after construction, or zero to complete
the operation.
.It Va rdip
Optional input/output node pointer, required with \fBDEVCTL_CONSTRUCT\fP.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
\fBndi_dc_devi_create()\fP constructs a persistent child of \fBpdip\fP from the nvlist
in \fBdcp\fP.
The nvlist must contain a string named \fBDC_DEVI_NODENAME\fP giving the node name.
Other supported nvpair types are \fBDATA_TYPE_INT32\fP, \fBDATA_TYPE_STRING\fP,
\fBDATA_TYPE_BYTE_ARRAY\fP, \fBDATA_TYPE_INT32_ARRAY\fP, and
\fBDATA_TYPE_STRING_ARRAY\fP; these are used to create hardware properties.
Other data types cause failure.
.Pp
With \fBDEVCTL_CONSTRUCT\fP in \fBflags\fP, the function returns a partially
constructed node without binding or attaching it.
In this mode \fBrdip\fP is required.
Initialize \fB*rdip\fP to \fBNULL\fP for a new node.
A later call may pass that node in \fB*rdip\fP to finish construction.
The output does not acquire an additional \fBndi_hold_devi()\fP reference.
.Pp
Without \fBDEVCTL_CONSTRUCT\fP, the function normally brings the child online.
If \fBDEVCTL_OFFLINE\fP is present in the request's own flags, it binds and
initializes the child while leaving it offline.
On success it stores the node in \fB*rdip\fP, if supplied.
If the request has a user output buffer, it copies the child's \fBname@address\fP
there, without a terminating null byte.
.Pp
Failure paths can remove the partially created node.
Do not assume a non-null output or input node pointer is still valid after
failure.
Hardware-property update statuses are not propagated by this helper, so
success does not guarantee that every property allocation succeeded.
.Sh CONTEXT
Call from user context when a user result buffer is supplied.
Otherwise the function may be called from user or kernel context.
It may sleep.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The function returns zero on success.
Errors include \fBEINVAL\fP for malformed properties or invalid construction
arguments, \fBENXIO\fP for binding or online failure, \fBENODEV\fP if no driver is
bound after online processing, \fBEBUSY\fP if offline notification is refused,
and \fBEFAULT\fP for a result-copy failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ndi_dc_allochdl 9F ,
.Xr ndi_devi_alloc 9F ,
.Xr ndi_devi_online 9F ,
.Xr ndi_prop_update 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F
